Old lots are A/input 0, new lots B/input 1; lot is unique, non-null and sorted ascending on both inputs. Output 0 goes to WithdrawnLotReview, output 1 to EstimateReview, output 2 to DiscoveredLotIntake. The two one-sided consumers start with the original respective rows. DiscoveredLotIntake must eventually add intake_label=DISCOVERED, which is absent from the input layouts. EstimateReview requires every shared lot with its new estimate and UP/DOWN/SAME relative to the old estimate. State any downstream step needed for the intake label.

Input A fields: lot:string!, estimate:integer!. Input B fields: lot:string!, estimate:integer!. Reconciliation consumer fields: lot:string!, estimate:integer!, movement:string!. A question mark marks nullable fields; ! marks required fields.

```ctl
//#CTL2
function integer transform() {
    $out.0.lot = $in.1.lot;
    $out.0.estimate = $in.1.estimate;
    if ($in.1.estimate > $in.0.estimate) $out.0.movement = "UP";
    else if ($in.1.estimate < $in.0.estimate) $out.0.movement = "DOWN";
    else $out.0.movement = "SAME";
    return ALL;
}
```

