Generate the CLOSE side of laboratory-method SCD2 changes in DataIntersection. Input 0 contains incoming methods, input 1 the current dimension. For unequal method values, produce the previous version with only its validity end/current flag changed. Other stages handle OPEN. For an equal method, emit nothing. effective_at is later than current valid_from; half-open intervals. Null and empty method differ. Join key $lab=$lab, ascending unique lab on both streams, default errorActions; physical output 1 feeds the closure writer.

Input 0: lab string non-null, method string nullable, effective_at date non-null; Input 1: lab string non-null, method string nullable, method_sk long non-null, valid_from date non-null. Output 0: lab string non-null, close_sk long non-null, method string nullable, valid_from date non-null, valid_to date non-null, is_current boolean non-null.

```ctl
//#CTL2
function integer transform() {
    if ($in.0.method == $in.1.method) return SKIP;
    $out.0.lab = $in.1.lab;
    $out.0.close_sk = $in.1.method_sk;
    $out.0.method = $in.1.method;
    $out.0.valid_from = $in.1.valid_from;
    $out.0.valid_to = $in.0.effective_at;
    $out.0.is_current = false;
    return ALL;
}
```

